"கழ","tr":"kaḻa"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"றுமிவ்","tr":"ṟumiv"}]},{"text":"வழுங்க","tr":"vaḻuṅka","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"வழுங்","tr":"vaḻuṅ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"க","tr":"ka"}]},{"text":"லூரே","tr":"lūrē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"லூ","tr":"lū"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ரே","tr":"rē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"எறும்பி","parts":[{"text":"எறும்பி","lemma":"eṟumpi","gloss":"ant"}],"gloss":"ant"},{"surface":"அளையின்","parts":[{"text":"அளை","lemma":"aḷai","gloss":"hole"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like the hole"},{"surface":"குறும்","parts":[{"text":"குறும்","lemma":"குறும்","gloss":"small"}],"gloss":"small","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பல்","parts":[{"text":"பல்","lemma":"பல்","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சுனைய","parts":[{"text":"சுனை","lemma":"cuṉai","gloss":"mountain pool"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having water pools"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உலைக்கல்","parts":[{"text":"உலை","lemma":"ulai","gloss":"furnace"},{"text":"கல்","lemma":"kal","gloss":"stone"}],"gloss":"anvil stone"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"aṉṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"பாறை","parts":[{"text":"பாறை","lemma":"pāṟai","gloss":"rock"}],"gloss":"rock"},{"surface":"ஏறி","parts":[{"text":"ஏறி","lemma":"ēṟi","gloss":"having climbed"}],"gloss":"having climbed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொடு","parts":[{"text":"கொடு","lemma":"koṭu","gloss":"curved"}],"gloss":"curved"},{"surface":"வில்","parts":[{"text":"வில்","lemma":"vil","gloss":"bow"}],"gloss":"bow"},{"surface":"எயினர்","parts":[{"text":"எயினர்","lemma":"eyiṉar","gloss":"hunters"}],"gloss":"hunters"},{"surface":"பகழி","parts":[{"text":"பகழி","lemma":"pakaḻi","gloss":"arrow"}],"gloss":"arrow"},{"surface":"மாய்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"மாய்க்கும்","lemma":"māy","gloss":"sharpening"}],"gloss":"sharpening"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கவலைத்து","parts":[{"text":"கவலை","lemma":"kavalai","gloss":"forked path"},{"text":"து","lemma":"tu","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having forked paths"},{"surface":"என்பவர்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"to say"},{"text":"பவர்","lemma":"pavar","gloss":"they who"}],"gloss":"those who say"},{"surface":"தேர்","parts":[{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"tēr","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"chariot"},{"surface":"சென்ற","parts":[{"text":"சென்ற","lemma":"சென்ற","gloss":"went"}],"gloss":"went","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஆறே","parts":[{"text":"ஆறு","lemma":"āṟu","gloss":"path"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"the path indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அது","parts":[{"text":"அது","lemma":"atu","gloss":"that"}],"gloss":"that"},{"surface":"மற்று","parts":[{"text":"மற்று","lemma":"maṟṟu","gloss":"expletive"}],"gloss":"and"},{"surface":"அவலம்","parts":[{"text":"அவலம்","lemma":"avalam","gloss":"distress"}],"gloss":"distress"},{"surface":"கொள்ளாது","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"koḷ","gloss":"to feel"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ātu","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without feeling"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நொதுமற்","parts":[{"text":"நொதுமற்","lemma":"நொதுமற்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கழறுமிவ்","parts":[{"text":"கழறுமிவ்","lemma":"கழறுமிவ்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வழுங்க","parts":[{"text":"வழுங்க","lemma":"வழுங்க","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"லூரே","parts":[{"text":"லூரே","lemma":"லூரே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Like the holes of ants, having small, many water pools, / climbing on the rocks that are like anvils, / curved-bow hunters sharpen their arrows, / \"it has forks,\" they say, the path where his chariot went! / Without feeling distress for that, / this noisy town rebukes like strangers.","translation":"They say the path where his chariot went is full of split ways, with many small water pools like ant-holes, where hunters with curved bows climb onto rocks like anvils to sharpen their arrows. Without feeling any sympathy for that hardship, this noisy town gossips like indifferent strangers.","modern":"எறும்புப் புற்றுத் துவாரங்களைப் போலச் சிறிய பல நீர்ச்சுனைகளைக் கொண்டதும், கொல்லனின் உலைக்களத்துக்கல் போன்ற பாறைகளின் மேல் ஏறி வளைந்த வில்லைக் கொண்ட எயினர்கள் தம் அம்புகளைக் கூர்மையாக்கும் பிரியும் வழிகளைக் கொண்டதுமானது தலைவன் தேர் சென்ற வழி என்று கூறுவர். அந்தத் துன்பத்தை எண்ணி வருந்தாமல், இந்த ஆரவாரமுடைய ஊரார் அயலாரைப் போலப் பழிதூற்றுகின்றனர்.","explanation":"The heroine is expressing her deep distress to her close friend. Her lover has departed on a journey through a harsh desert path (pālai tiṇai) to earn wealth. People describe the path he took as perilous, filled with split paths, where fierce hunters climb anvil-like rocks to sharpen their arrows, and where water is scarce, found only in tiny pools resembling ant-holes. Instead of showing compassion for her anxiety over his dangerous journey, the people of this noisy town gossip and reproach her like indifferent strangers. The contrast between the harshness of the desert path and the cold indifference of the town highlights her isolation and sorrow.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}